        </ezobject:attribute>
        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="391" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
              <embed size="original" view="embed" align="center" object_remote_id="ezdemo-img-blog-velocity"/>
            </paragraph>
            <paragraph>Most PHP applications start from scratch on every request. Velocity starts Exponential once, keeps it warm in memory and hands each request to a worker that is ready to go.</paragraph>
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>What changes for you</header>
                <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Pages render faster, especially the first byte.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">The server is configured like Debian's Apache, so administrators feel at home.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <paragraph xmlns:tmp="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/temporary/">Deploying a change is one command that reloads what changed.</paragraph>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
